  "description": "The idempotency and terminal cells of the §3.4 state x operation matrix, driven through the store as a crashing-then-retrying client would hit them. A second expose of an already-exposed reservation returns the record and leaves exposedTotal at 5, not 10. A second commit returns the existing entry and does not re-increment cumulativeCommitted. Once A is committed, a fresh expose is refused as TX402_CONFIG_INVALID (reservation-already-terminal). On a second reservation B, release(exposed) frees the exposed amount and a replayed release returns the released record unchanged. The final snapshot shows every amount resolved into exactly one term.",
